# Paths the privacy check skips: third-party code vendored whole, whose author and contact lines are already public
# upstream and cannot be edited without modifying the vendored source. One glob per line, matched against the
# repo-relative path. First-party code never goes here; a single legitimate line carries `privacy-check: allow`.

# libwebp, copied verbatim by media-webp/native/update-source.sh, and the headers the iOS cinterop takes from it.
# One glob, because the history also holds both from before the module was renamed from webp to media-webp.
*/libwebp/*

# Agent skills the story-tools installer copies from a public skills repository and overwrites on every refresh, so a
# line in them cannot carry the allow marker: the ones .agents/skills/MANAGED.md lists, by name. A project's own skill
# beside them is first-party and is checked, and so is a skill the installer adds until it is listed here.
.agents/skills/story-workflow/*
.agents/skills/story-reconcile/*
.agents/skills/to-issues/*
.agents/skills/triage/*
.agents/skills/project-docs/*
.agents/skills/to-prd/*
.agents/skills/to-adr/*
.agents/skills/to-rad/*
.agents/skills/grill-with-docs/*
.agents/skills/regulatory-compliance/*
.agents/skills/handoff/*
.agents/skills/housekeeping/*
.agents/skills/zoom-out/*
.agents/skills/tdd/*
.agents/skills/improve-codebase-architecture/*
.agents/skills/to-ux/*
.agents/skills/write-a-skill/*
